{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness","id":937378,"title":"Your view on the World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-25T17:14:21-07:00","id":937378,"title":"Your view on the World of Darkness?","content":"Since Chronicles of Darkness is quite modular setting, it's interesting how you see the world itself?<br /> As for me, I think that World of Darkness should be... you know... dark)) So, I see the following points^<br /> 1) High lethality (like, we have no 'official' statistic, so in my headcanon it like 'among all nub-supernatural creatures only half of them survive first 5 years, and the next 5 years will survive only half of the first half' But THAN the statistic curve flattens - cuz victims turn to hunters.<br /> 2) Social structure - a medieval (or gangster/cartel) mentality/ Like, small groups, strong unity inside (cuz you can't trust somebody except your bros and sis), strong xenophobia to outsiders (any stranger is an enemy or at very least suspicious - till prove otherwise). To guys from other splats, the same xenophobiaX2. Lot of cruel moments (Vendetta and mutual responsibility lead to such cute things like 'for fail of the one all his/her family and friends will be slayed - and their age, sex and pregnancy stage is irrelevant'). &quot;Kill or be killed&quot;, &quot;right of the power&quot; and other principles work directly.<br /> The world operates according to the laws of dark crime drama<br /> So, such violence is a normal here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SV7h6NDLnCI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SV7h6NDLnCI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SV7h6NDLnCI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SV7h6NDLnCI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for qulity, i didn't found better.<br /> So, how you see your WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T17:29:50-07:00","id":937380,"title":"","content":"Relatively closer to shows like Fringe and X-Files or SG-1. There's weird stuff, it happens, it gets covers up because people either don't pay attention or couldn't believe it if you showed them pieces of evidence. It's not as overall dark as the books make it, but in exchange, in my settings, almost every official and every fan-splat exists and is operating against the others. Including children of gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T17:48:59-07:00","id":937387,"title":"","content":"Dark. Not as in <i>hopeless</i>, but as in <i>creepy</i>. Not grey, but dark shades of vibrant colors. There's lot of genuine happy and peaceful lives out there that aren't destroyed by evil monsters/fellow man. But even those feel or remember something creepy out there; not exactly watching and leering at them (those are usually the victims), but just... <i>there</i>. We pretend they're not but we don't go out on full moons 'just in case'. As the hyspanic saying goes 'non creo en brujas pero que las hay las hay'.<br /> <br /> Also limited settings. Usually humans and splat-less monsters (maybe even including splat-less versions of the usual guys), or splat-centric world with appropriate other monster conforming to it (mostly unexplainable or cthulian cryptids and mortal witches, warlocks and sorcerers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:14:06-07:00","id":937402,"title":"","content":"As a result of my players, my games invariably skew toward horror comedy much of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:45:18-07:00","id":937441,"title":"","content":"Slice of life. At the end of day, it's just life, going on. Sometimes the dark is violent, oppressive, bitter, maddening, tragic. Sometimes the dark is a midnight sky in July as people are passing around the watermelon and smore materials.<br /> <br /> You don't know what sort of night will fall, only that it will, and that it too will pass. It's people who get stuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:56:05-07:00","id":937450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=937441#post937441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slice of life. At the end of day, it's just life, going on. Sometimes the dark is violent, oppressive, bitter, maddening, tragic. Sometimes the dark is a midnight sky in July as people are passing around the watermelon and smore materials.<br /> <br /> You don't know what sort of night will fall, only that it will, and that it too will pass. It's people who get stuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I play it more or less like real life with supernatural shit thrown into the mix- Masquerade and all -here and there. All in all though I think the world is plenty dark without me trying to prove to my players how edgy I am at all times BECAUSE IT JUST ISN'T GRIMDARK ENOUGH. And to a fair extent, real life writes the plot since I take inspiration and story ideas from newspaper articles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T23:02:16-07:00","id":937491,"title":"","content":"While some people might find the comparison odd because of the lack of overt supernatural elements. For me, True Detective Season 1 still remains the seminal Chronicles of Darkness on film for me. Every scene has an air of sinister implication and Mcconaughey's character acts as a wonderful gateway as someone you feel has stepped into the horrors hiding under the surface in contrast to Harrelson's character dealing with his own demons even as he's lead into darker waters. Plus the villain makes for an excellent Slasher and the season as a whole screams Hunter the Vigil to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:25:00-07:00","id":937586,"title":"","content":"My vision of the World/Chronicles of Darkness lacks the supernatural (at least at the moment...<i>Second Sight</i> looks intriguing, though), but I'm in the planning stages of my first ever campaign using the system. So far, it looks like an amalgamation of the following:<br /> <br /> <i>Daredevil </i>Netflix series<br /> <i>No Country for Old Men<br /> The Counselor<br /> The Departed<br /> Bad Lieutenant</i><br /> maybe even a little of Nolan's <i>Dark Knight </i>series","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:22:11-07:00","id":937636,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xLGKdW3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">This picture sums up a lot of my feelings.</a><br /> <br /> Dark, isolated, yet intriguing; pockets of light that provide context and give you the curiosity to go wandering into the dark to explore. My games usually go High Weirdness and wander in and out of the transmundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T13:46:20-07:00","id":937750,"title":"","content":"Black Lagoon with fangs. Action-packed and over-the-top while still being cool.<br /> <br /> \u200bDark, but not hopelessly so. Violent, but survivable, and overall, my WoD games skew more towards action-horror and politics and away from personal horror. That's what I like in my games and that's how I roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T14:47:07-07:00","id":937779,"title":"","content":"The personal horror of Chronicles is probably one of my favorite things about the game.<br /> <br /> I'm big on the general concept of the recognition of flaws and the acceptance of damning factors. Really, personal stories about coping with the terrible, learning to abandon them or transform them into the wonderful or find the healthiest way to go with it-those are the things I like. A character's external struggles are fun to watch and all, but they don't mean as much to me if I don't get the pleasure of knowing that they were once terrified of who they are or were or what they did, that they are angry at themselves or sad at themselves, how the world wounds them-how they'll do those things again and again, how it keeps happening-and how, these fights, these moments, are about them reclaiming themselves, transforming into more or greater, or even something worse but is wholly theirs.<br /> <br /> I don't like escapism. It has its' place, its' uses. But a crazy shoot-out lacks punch if someone's not descending into or arising out of the abyss. I want to know how the shoot-out is transforming them, not how many bodies are hitting the floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T23:13:45-07:00","id":937951,"title":"","content":"It's a universe without cause or reason, the supernatural is there for the same reason the natural is, a complicated culmination of random events. Most understand this, and it scares them into clinging to some belief or another that makes sense of the world and promises some greater meaning.<br /> <br /> The supernatural is wildly prevalent, everyone's been touched by it, though in most cases it's nothing as obvious as an encounter with a vampire. More often it's something like Thomas Ligotti's Gas Station Carnivals, a lingering tension constantly itching at that reminder that the universe isn't how they try to think it is, isn't safe or even meant for them.<br /> <br /> Taking some cues from the old World of Darkness, it's our world but worse, just as its our world but more mysterious. The tension drives most people to extremes. Maybe they hide out, find some safe niche with people like themselves and never leave it, the whole group growing more and more bitter at the outsiders. Or maybe they act out, stealing money from their bosses, employees, friends, family, gang, cult. Some see ways to seize control of things and go after that. There's a heavy sense of desperation the closer you get to the heart of the cities, and the wilds a sort of eerie fraying, as the things people cling to are farther and farther away and the truth of the senselessness of the world becomes harder to deny. <br /> <br /> Like Lashet, I have the 'mortality' rate high, even among supernaturals, with most either dying or losing themselves to whatever their version of 0 Humanity is. Vampires sometimes just disappear, thought to have traveled to another city or fallen into torpor and are never heard from again. Werewolves who fall in holes in time or Shadow are thought to have died in battle against some unseen enemy. Among the supernaturals I try to play up the lack of knowledge about 'other places.' There's strange, scary tales about not-so-far-off lands. A city in the next state where the Circle follows a hideous Blood Moon that grants them the power to convert other vampires to its worship. A town of werewolves somewhere down the highway who serve a Firstborn no one's ever heard of that hunts Forsaken and Pure with them in the flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:35:16-07:00","id":937981,"title":"","content":"I use the following quote to pitch the setting to any prospective players:<br /> &quot;What are you prepared to do to survive tonight and will you be able to live with it come morning?&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone knows somethings up but they keep their heads down and try not to grab any unwanted attention. Life is scary enough without thinking about the paranormal. The vampire who tried to drain you in that alley was &quot;just&quot; a ordinary mugger, the witch who read your fate and said you'll die in 7 days was just a hack psychic. And the thing that took your infant son from his crib last night? What are you talking about you never had a son! Now take your medication and get some sleep.<br /> <br /> Every part of the World of Darkness is an isolated state. Similar to a feudal kingdom. What's happening in New York is not happening in Tokyo. Large cities have factions of monsters politicking and sabotaging each other. Small towns usually only have a local pack of werewolves or a couple of vamps who hunt in the night. And in isolated rural areas things are completely unique. A cult in Loch Ness drowns sacrifices so they can get safe passage to the underworld. A group of werecoyotes cause car wrecks on the desert highways of Arizona as a practical joke only they get. And in the jungles of the Philipines, things called Tikbalangs jump down from the trees and grab passerby and bring them up to their nests. It's our world reflected through a fractured mirror, you still recognize it but the image is unfocused and distorted.<br /> <br /> The stories are intensely personal. Few &quot;save the world&quot; stories here. Underground factions fight each other for supremacy but there is no one power controlling everything, there are a million tiny conspiracies all tripping over one another.<br /> <br /> In general I see the setting as resembling contemporary shows like True Detective, Black Mirror, Utopia, and Hannibal. <br /> <br /> For more urban settings I think of the works of Thomas Ligotti and Franz Kafka. For wilderness settings I think of the carnivorous horror of Laird Barron. <br /> <br /> Basically the Chronicles of Darkness is one gaping maw that will swallow you and spit you back up as a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 07-27-2016, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T05:48:48-07:00","id":938046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=937779#post937779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The personal horror of Chronicles is probably one of my favorite things about the game.<br /> <br /> I'm big on the general concept of the recognition of flaws and the acceptance of damning factors. Really, personal stories about coping with the terrible, learning to abandon them or transform them into the wonderful or find the healthiest way to go with it-those are the things I like. A character's external struggles are fun to watch and all, but they don't mean as much to me if I don't get the pleasure of knowing that they were once terrified of who they are or were or what they did, that they are angry at themselves or sad at themselves, how the world wounds them-how they'll do those things again and again, how it keeps happening-and how, these fights, these moments, are about them reclaiming themselves, transforming into more or greater, or even something worse but is wholly theirs.<br /> <br /> I don't like escapism. It has its' place, its' uses. But a crazy shoot-out lacks punch if someone's not descending into or arising out of the abyss. I want to know how the shoot-out is transforming them, not how many bodies are hitting the floor.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bYou do bring up some good points. Guess I never thought of things that way,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T07:15:09-07:00","id":938089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=937491#post937491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some people might find the comparison odd because of the lack of overt supernatural elements. For me, True Detective Season 1 still remains the seminal Chronicles of Darkness on film for me. Every scene has an air of sinister implication and Mcconaughey's character acts as a wonderful gateway as someone you feel has stepped into the horrors hiding under the surface in contrast to Harrelson's character dealing with his own demons even as he's lead into darker waters. Plus the villain makes for an excellent Slasher and the season as a whole screams Hunter the Vigil to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this one, it's the same for me. In my chronicles the world is not such much darker as the real world, but you are gonna be confronted with the darker and darkest parts. There is enough death, violence and abuse out there, if you add the supernatural too it and just let your characters explore, there is plenty of horror for them. I also like the contrast, most people get perfectly by and live a normal life by just looking away too often. If the players are the people who cannot or will not look away and get deeper and deeper into the darkness, it's even more horrifying if the rest of the world tells you everything is alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:53:26-07:00","id":938150,"title":"","content":"Honestly?<br /> <br /> I have trouble taking it seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:46:08-07:00","id":938177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=938150#post938150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<br /> <br /> I have trouble taking it seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular reason?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to start an argument or anything: I agree that there are some downright silly elements in all of the gamelines, I've just always thought that the goofier elements juxtaposed with the dark stuff created a jarring, repulsive quality that I find amazing. Compare <i>High School of the Dead</i> and its buxom schoolgirl protagonists in a legitimately horrific, visceral situation: yeah, there's frankly stupid amounts of fanservice, but when scenes transition from fanservice to zombies tearing teenagers apart it feels so lurid that I feel guilty watching it.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm a big fan of mood whiplash and <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FridgeHorror\" target=\"_blank\">fridge horror</a> in my CofD.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that describes how I like to do things in my CofD. There aren't a lot of in-between situations in my games: I've had PCs go straight from tense survival-stealth sections to relaxed character moments to lethal combats without any sort of transition scenes in between. The characters should feel like their lives jump back and forth between pleasant and horrifying, and more often than not they should be the reason things are horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T22:19:07-07:00","id":942498,"title":"","content":"I've never owned the Innocents book but...well...just started watching Stranger Things today...and holy hell....so amazingly ChrOd. It has to be on the inspirational media for the next game line coming out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:04:12-07:00","id":942884,"title":"","content":"To me, one of the central themes, probably the closest thing there is to a Grand Unifying Principle of the Supernatural is &quot;there's always a cost&quot;. All power damages the user in some way, be it literally or through subtler means such as isolation. Growth is loss. To become an adult, you must lose the bliss and innocence of childhood. All change follows the same rules. Power, in all its forms, makes you less human. That's not to say that this is an objectively a bad thing. Human =\\= good and inhuman =\\= bad. But to truly, wisely use power, you have to be willing to make that trade. There's no such thing as a &quot;higher&quot; being, only parallel beings. Mages are not &quot;higher&quot; than normal humans, they are parallel: they paid a cost in humanity for their power. This isn't a personal philosophy of mine in general, it's just something I think is necessary for a horror setting. <br /> <br /> About splats, I think anyone, Onyx Path or fan, who wants to make a new splat should always ask two questions before they do: <br /> <br /> 1. Is this a recognizable type of monster or horror archetype, and 2. Does it deserve more representation in ChroD than it already has?<br /> <br /> About the setting itself, I think others have described it better and more eloquently, but I generally see it as a place with more crime and corruption and disaster than our world, but in a subtler way than the apocalyptic oWoD. Lots of crimes go unreported or ignored, lots of people disappear. People recognize on some unconscious level how tenuous everything is, and this is what keeps most people from investigating strange events or inconsistencies. Everyone has had some sort of brush, however brief, with the paranormal, but most forget about it and most of the others tell themselves that it had to have a rational explanation, even if they don't know what it is. A few believe this, but a lot of them tell themselves that to cover up the real reason why they never tried to pry into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:13:51-07:00","id":942899,"title":"","content":"In my CofD games, the multiverse is very Cthulhu-Mythos-like in that the Exarchs didn't oust benevolent Old Gods: the Old Gods were <i>always</i> monsters. Maybe not evil, per se, but still monstrous and grossly indifferent to human welfare. And the Fallen World is little better: the Shadow Realm is full of monomaniacal spirits that are slaves to their natures (even Luna and Helios) and so cannot demonstrate qualities they do not already embody.<br /> <br /> Goodness is something <i>human</i>. It's a treasure our species has, that the gods don't even know they're lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:03:28-07:00","id":943663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=942899#post942899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goodness is something <i>human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really enjoy the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HumansAreSpecial\" target=\"_blank\">Humans are Special</a> trope. Be it good or bad, but there's something <i>special</i> about mankind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T19:36:33-07:00","id":944083,"title":"","content":"See, I don't really like the idea that goodness is a quantifiable thing that you either are or aren't. I prefer the Wanda Pierce view: good isn't something you are, it's something you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:43:52-07:00","id":944406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=944083#post944083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't really like the idea that goodness is a quantifiable thing that you either are or aren't. I prefer the Wanda Pierce view: good isn't something you are, it's something you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. What I meant is, &quot;Humans have the <i>capacity</i> for good.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:28:01-07:00","id":946312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=938177#post938177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>I once heard a story from one of my friends about someone they knew (who had schizophrenia) who laughed her way through horror movies. They asked her why, once, and her response was that they were <i>hilarious</i> in comparison to her hallucinations.<br /> <br /> I'm not schizophrenic (I don't think, at least), but I still laugh at the Chronicles of Darkness. They try <i>too</i> hard, in my mind, and I think they're less miserable than my day-to-day. When the only body language you can read is disgust and anger, and you have to wear baffles to block out your senses because your brain doesn't <i>do</i> that... the &quot;personal horror&quot; of a lot of the splats looks downright <i>pleasant</i>.<br /> <br /> I can accept the game as a kinda-dingy urban fantasy game, but asking me to call it horror is asking a <i>bit</i> too much from me. To be honest, hanging around here just kind of cements that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:51:59-07:00","id":946430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness?p=938150#post938150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<br /> <br /> I have trouble taking it seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm happy that I've found someone who finally agrees with me here!<br /> <br /> I find that the only WoD games I can take seriously are the ones that don't base themselves on <i>personal </i>horror, and instead on some other form of horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:13:37-07:00","id":946535,"title":"","content":"Well for the supernatural splats, I'll be very boring and say the world is basically that implied by the metaphysics of their condition and powers and what is described as the thematic fulcrum in their cores, i.e. for Mages the world is a dangerous tempting mystery, for Vampires it's about the balance of what you were vs what you're becoming, for Werewolves it's an unending animistic hunt.<br /> <br /> The only real one I had difficulty with was mortals, but I basically think of it like our world, except most small groups of people have experiences something like <b><i>Stranger Things</i></b>, i.e. an odd encounter with the supernatural that everybody forgets about on purpose/has to move on from, with nobody really being able to learn enough or get enough people to open up to really start concluding things about the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:33:43-07:00","id":948275,"title":"","content":"My games take a lot of cues from shows like Supernatural, and Penny Dreadful. Everything is uncertain; folks are generally liars and cheats; monsters are highly involved in daily life; missing is worse than dead; and violence is quick, brutal and lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:42:30-07:00","id":958142,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this counts as thread necromancy, but I had some thoughts I wanted to share.<br /> <br /> Fundamentally, I play the World of Darkness as a World Half-Full.<br /> There is fear and suffering in abundance, with secrets and shadows so deep that -nobody- will ever learn all of it. It is a large and terrifying world, where people suffer even more than in our own. But there is hope.<br /> There is hope that if people work together and work hard, things may get better. That through determination and struggle, the world will become a better place. It could get better, or fall further still. The hope exists to make the horror even worse and the horror exists to make the hope brighter. There is a catharsis in that conflict. There is worth and value in this fallen world, but it's a struggle to keep it alive.<br /> <br /> I tend to view it more as exceedingly dark fantasy, then allow the horror to naturally emerge. The world is too large to be confined to the genre of horror alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:57:44-07:00","id":958148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/937378-your-view-on-the-world-of-darkness#post937378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Chronicles of Darkness is quite modular setting, it's interesting how you see the world itself?</div> </div> </div> </div> As the real world + magic. The Darkness part is just what happens in the cracks of human society, generally hidden from view. That tactic understanding by humanity to ignore the occult and the monsters is the only difference between a real world person and the CofD people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:18:18-07:00","id":958157,"title":"","content":"In my games, the cities in World of Darkness are basically Gotham from the Batman Begins (2005) movie. A city torn apart by urban decay, crime and corruption. Furthermore, there are rumours of vampire-like monsters moving in the shadows and manipulating things, that many people fear, but few actually want to belief are real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}